The getter is already minimal, so the only remaining win is to let the compiler treat it as a pure/leaf accessor: marking it `const` (and hinting `hot`) allows call-site CSE, better scheduling, and avoids reloading the member across repeated calls without changing any observable behaviour.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 FieldDefinition::GetType() const
{
    return type;
}
